**EXHIBIT A: CONTRACTUAL TERMS AND CONDITIONS FOR MILITARY SYSTEMS SUPPLY AND SUPPORT**

**Contract No.: MSL-2023-0456**  
**Effective Date:** January 15, 2024  
**Parties:**  
1. **Advanced Defense Technologies, Inc.** (hereinafter referred to as "ADT"), a corporation organized under the laws of Virginia, with principal offices located at 1234 Military Ave, Arlington, VA 22202.  
2. **Department of Defense** (hereinafter referred to as "DoD"), an agency of the United States government, located at 1400 Defense Pentagon, Washington, D.C. 20301.  

**1. Scope of Work:**  
ADT shall deliver and support the following military systems and equipment (hereinafter referred to as "the Equipment") as specified in Attachment 1:  
   a. **Advanced Combat Drones** (ACD Model X-2024)  
   b. **Secure Communication Systems** (SCS Model C-300)  
   c. **Surveillance Radar Systems** (SRS Model R-500)  

**2. Delivery Schedule:**  
The Equipment shall be delivered to **Fort Bragg, NC 28310** no later than **March 30, 2024**. The first batch (10 units of ACD) must be operational by **April 15, 2024**, with subsequent deliveries scheduled on a bi-weekly basis.

**3. Payment Terms:**  
Total contract value is **$15,000,000**, payable as follows:  
   a. 30% upon signature of this contract,  
   b. 40% upon delivery of the first batch,  
   c. 30% upon completion of operational testing and acceptance by **General Mark Thompson** of **U.S. Army**.  

**4. Support and Maintenance:**  
ADT agrees to provide maintenance and operational support for a period of **two years** post-delivery, including training for **50 personnel** from the **Army’s 82nd Airborne Division**. This will include specialized training on the SCS and ongoing technical support via the **National Defense Network**.

